# =============================================================================
# bizgraph example data. ALL NAMES AND IDENTIFIERS ARE SYNTHETIC: the ABNs,
# ACNs and LEIs pass their checksums but were generated for this file and
# are not meant to describe any real business or person.
#
# Plain Turtle so every tool can read it; the "GRAPH" comment above each block
# names the named graph the exporter would write it into.
#
# Contents
#   A. Snapshot descriptions (one per source graph)
#   B. Source records
#   C. Canonical parties (incl. a person, and the deliberate violation:
#      ACN 610005555 claimed by two organisations with different names)
#   D. Facts: cancelled AFSL, ban on a person, GLEIF ownership chain
#      SCA -> Beta -> Gamma -> Beta (3 levels, cycles at the top),
#      an affiliation, an unattributed ACCC notice, a trusteeship whose
#      trustee is named only by ACN
#   E. Links and an abstention (matcher version m-2026.11.1)
# Expected SHACL result: exactly two violations, both from the ACN
# uniqueness constraint, focus nodes urn:abn:23610005555 and
# urn:abn:55610004441. Everything else conforms, including the cycle.
# =============================================================================

